; todo-v02-open.sabra — the v0.2 filter query: prelude accessors only.
;
; The 12.5 query reached for first/second/rec-val on numeric keys;
; v0.2 names the fields (todo-entry todo-state todo-title todo-open).
; Same reach, no calculus: filter the entry list by state, collect the
; titles in board order.
;
; SHAPE NOTE (probe-found, 2026-10-02; DISPOSITIONED 2026-10-04, see
; FINDINGS.md non-F): the original note dodged two defects that did not
; reproduce on re-drive - the recorded repros were mis-shaped inputs (a
; flat kv list is one multi-field record, not a list of records;
; list-append's second argument was a bare element).  The composition
; below keeps its lambdas INLINE and its def applications DIRECT, which
; remains correct and harmless; the three-engine corpus rows
; dialect_list-map-defarg / -flat / dialect_list-append-order now pin
; both shapes as known answers.  The collection still rides an inline
; pair-prepend list-fold: list-fold traverses right-to-left, so the
; prepend preserves board order (pinned, not a defect).

(lambda (prefix)
  (let ((open-items
          (list-filter
            (lambda (entry)
              (tree-eq (todo-state (todo-entry entry)) todo-open))
            (prim "tree/list" prefix))))
    (list-fold
      (lambda (entry) (lambda (acc) (pair (todo-title (todo-entry entry)) acc)))
      0
      open-items)))
